        "message": "feat(engine): cloud-calibrated factor veto + unified cloud data layer (2.0.0, vc13)\n\nThree additions to the engine chain, each traceable to cloud data that already\nexisted but the app never used.\n\n1. CloudFeed - one entry point for cloud data\n   Before: every module built its own URL and connection; EngineFeed alone did 8\n   sequential openConnection calls and silently dropped failures into `missing`.\n   Now: a Doc registry, concurrent fetch, in-memory TTL cache, staleness judged\n   from each file's own ts, and fallback to the previous snapshot on failure.\n   EngineFeed.loadAll() now goes through it, so one dead file no longer stalls or\n   blanks the other seven.\n\n2. FactorWeightStrategy - cloud weights, on-device indicators\n   weight_calibration.json carries per-indicator rel_weight from weight_calibrator_v3\n   (50k-60k samples, 16 indicators). The app had the indicators (Donchian, Ultimate,\n   Choppiness, CMO, Keltner, VWMA, A/D, HullMA, Pivot, MA, SuperTrend, ElderForce,\n   Vortex, MACD, RSI, RSV) but never used the calibration - it scored stocks with\n   hardcoded thresholds.\n   Deliberately framed as **veto, not selection**: cloud data shows all 16 have\n   negative edge and bull_win_rate of 43-45%, and market_advice is avoid_first.\n   So a stock only gets AVOID / WATCH / PASS - \"PASS\" means \"not vetoed here\", not\n   \"buy\". An early version returned BUY for the three rising fixtures; that was\n   wrong given the bull base rate, and the test now asserts the down-trending\n   fixture is vetoed instead.\n   Also fixed local indicator gaps: ExtendedIndicators.superTrend has the upper and\n   lower bands swapped, so the strategy uses its own corrected version; MACD / RSI /\n   RSV / A-D slope are implemented here because the module's versions are private\n   or terminal-value only.\n\n3. SignalCalibration - OOS and regime as a gate, not decoration\n   walkforward.json (45 folds, IS 47.2% -> OOS 48.6%) and market_advice=avoid_first\n   now produce two coefficients: confidence (overfit rule taken from the cloud's own\n   \"OOS < IS - 10pp\" threshold) and buyFactor. positionFactor is their product and\n   is only ever applied downward. The decision screen chain is now explicit:\n   cloud cap -> ETF share adjustment -> calibration gate, each step labelled.\n\nCap chain note: applyCap maps a *base* cap to a calibrated one and must not be\ncalled twice (0.85 x 0.85). The test asserts monotonic decrease rather than\nidempotence, and the doc comment says so.\n\nTests: engine now has a JVM test source set with 4 real 140-bar klines\n(688655, 002230, 600519, 601398) plus the actual cloud calibration fixtures.\nCI runs :engine:test in the engine gate - compiling alone would not catch\n\"weights parsed as equal\" or \"downtrend read as buy\".",
